title: Panel chrome
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

! Panel chrome decision + revert option

The view panel chassis (`$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/ui/ViewTemplate/view-body`) is a styled
`<fieldset class="tc-tiddler-info gsd-info-mod hgsd-panel-fieldset">` with no legend.

!! Why

* The panel genuinely groups a set of related form controls — a fieldset is the honest element.
* `.tc-tiddler-info` (vanilla theme) supplies padding, background and top/bottom hairlines; the plugin rule completes a full 1px border box in the `tiddler-info-border` colour, turning the panel into a deliberate card.
* The descendant rule `.hgsd-panel-fieldset fieldset { … }` structurally resets nested fieldsets (the status radios, and any future or third-party semantic groups) so they inherit clean styling with zero per-section classes.

!! Reverting to the pre-chrome hairline strip

If you prefer the old look (top/bottom hairlines only, no side borders), change the
`.hgsd-panel-fieldset` rule in `ui/stylesheet/sections.tid` to:

```
.hgsd-panel-fieldset {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-info-border>>;
    border-bottom: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-info-border>>;
    min-width: 0;
}
```

`.tc-tiddler-info` already paints exactly those two hairlines, so this restores the
original appearance while keeping the fieldset semantics and the nested-fieldset reset.

!! Related flip: modal Attributes chrome

The modal's Attributes container is `<fieldset class="hgsd-modal-attributes">` with a
visible `<legend>` and no border. To chrome it like the panel instead, change its
`border: 0` reset in `ui/stylesheet/sections.tid` to the same bordered rule as
`.hgsd-panel-fieldset`.